                "id": "finite-game",
                "body_md": "Fix a finite universe $N$. A game $g:\\mathcal P(N)\\to\\mathbb R$ has output baseline $b=g(\\varnothing)$ and interaction $I_g(A)=\\sum_{U\\subseteq A}(-1)^{|A|-|U|}g(U)$. Write $w_A=I_g(A)$. Every subset sum includes the empty set, and $w_\\varnothing=b$. The finite difference is $\\Delta_Tg(S)=\\sum_{L\\subseteq T}(-1)^{|T|-|L|}g(L\\cup S)$. No zero output baseline is assumed. Centering $g_0=g-b$ removes only the empty dividend."
