                "title": "Specialize the shared weighted identity to order one",
                "body_md": "The target $T$ and its external environment $E$ are disjoint. At $k=1$, each left weight agrees with the original SII definition and each right weight is $1/(|U|+1)$. For $T=N$, the environment is empty and the result is $w_N$. For an empty target, the left side is the indicated weighted average of raw outputs and the right side includes the empty dividend $b$.",
