        "original_statement_md": "The paper lists: (1) sparsity — few salient interactions on a specific sample; (2) universal matching — output on any masked sample is well matched by specific interactions; (3) sample-wise transferability — salient interactions are shared across different samples in the same category. The empirical observations are attributed to Li & Zhang (2023b).",
