                "body_md": "The source theorem occurs in Case 1, where $|\\eta^{(k)}|\\gg1/n$ excludes complete cancellation. Put $B_k=\\sum_{|S|=k}|I(S)|$, $\\eta^{(k)}=A^{(k)}/B_k$, and $\\tau>0$, and let $R^{(k)}$ count the terms with $|I(S)|\\ge\\tau$. In this original range, $B_k>0$ and $\\eta^{(k)}\\ne0$, so $\\tau R^{(k)}\\le\\sum_{|S|=k,|I(S)|\\ge\\tau}|I(S)|\\le B_k=|A^{(k)}|/|\\eta^{(k)}|$.",
