                "id": "iclr2024-sparse-noise-linearity-step-1",
                "title": "Definitions, original target, and premise adapter",
                "body_md": "If g′(S)=g(S)+ε_S, then g′₀(S)=g₀(S)+(ε_S−ε_empty). Set e₀(S)=ε_S−ε_empty and distribute the finite sum:\n$I_{g'_0}(S)=\\sum_{T\\subseteq S}(-1)^{|S|-|T|}[g_0(T)+e_0(T)]=I_{g_0}(S)+I_{e_0}(S)$.\nBoth empty interactions vanish. For nonempty S the constant ε_empty has zero alternating coefficient, so the noise coefficient is also $\\sum_{T\\subseteq S}(-1)^{|S|-|T|}\\varepsilon_T$. This needs no independence and implies no variance amplification. The insufficient source variance premise remains separate. Use the compiled `interaction_add` and `interaction_centered_nonempty`.",
                "formula_tex": "I′(S)=I(S)+\\sum_{T\\subseteq S}(-1)^{|S|-|T|}(\\varepsilon_T-\\varepsilon_\\varnothing).",
