                "title": "Definitions, original target, and premise adapter",
                "body_md": "Use one model $v(z)=\\sum_{i=1}^n z_i$, zero input baseline, and samples $x^{(j)}=e_j$. Every sample output is $1$, so threshold classification $v(z)>1/2$ puts all samples in the same positive class and satisfies the original same-class setting. Their centered masked games are $g_0^{(j)}(S)=\\mathbf1_{j\\in S}$. Pure-singleton coefficient distribution gives $I^{(j)}(\\{j\\})=1$ with all other coefficients zero. Each sample is maximally sparse and reconstructs every mask exactly, but different samples have disjoint salient families. The model needs only $n$ singleton patterns, rather than an exponential number. This refutes the source inference without adding a pattern-budget assumption to replace it.",
