                "title": "Definitions, original target, and premise adapter",
                "body_md": "The final source decomposition is g₀(S)=g_∧(S)+g_∨(S), with both components zero at empty. Apply the Möbius transform to g_∧ and the reversed OR definition to g_∨. This is externally cited and has no new detailed local author proof. The shared reconstructions require the same finite universe, one fixed decomposition for every mask, zero component empty values, and the separately defined zero OR empty coefficient. They give $g_\\land(S)=\\sum_{T\\subseteq S}I_\\land(T)$ and $g_\\lor(S)=\\sum_{T\\cap S\\ne\\varnothing}I_\\lor(T)$; add them to obtain Eq. (62). The component-name and γ-sign misprints in the parameter sentence are recorded at the algorithm-formula level and do not alter this final matching proposition.",
