          "en": {
            "title": "The complete six-token interaction-extraction example",
            "overview": "The example records input domains, baseline, 64 masks, log odds, gamma, interactions, optimization and thresholding. It is an algorithm example rather than a general correctness proof.",
            "proof_steps": [],
            "source_material_summary_md": "Appendix L gives eight steps. (1) Use the six tokens in A stitch in time saves nine, with token embeddings in $\\mathbb R^{768}$ for BERTBASE or $\\mathbb R^{1024}$ for BERTLARGE. (2) Choose each model special-token embedding as its baseline. (3) Enumerate all $2^6=64$ masks, from $T_0=\\varnothing$ to $T_{63}=N$. (4) Evaluate each masked model output as log odds of the ground-truth class. (5) Set AND and OR components to half the output plus or minus gamma for every model and mask. (6) Compute interactions using Eqs. (1) and (2); although the printed step includes all indices, the OR empty value must still follow the separate Section 2.1 convention. (7) Learn gamma using Eq. (6) and iterate from step 5 to convergence. (8) Select each model salient family using the absolute-interaction threshold. This is an algorithm example, not a proof of convergence or general correctness.",
            "notation_map": []
          }
