                "title": "Represent shared nodes and skip connections",
                "body_md": "A finite feed-forward graph can be unfolded in topological order into a finite expression tree, repeating shared subexpressions without changing their values. The finite-child block syntax admits any already built child expression, including skip connections, and does not assume disjoint child fields.",
