              {
                "id": "hnet-count-eq9",
                "title": "Check the centered boundary of source Equation (9)",
                "body_md": "Equation (9) prints the raw output as the sum of its centered dividends, then as retained dividends plus their omitted tail. Definition 2 makes that sum the output difference from the baseline. For a traditional network with a nonzero baseline the first equality is false: the constant-one model has zero centered dividends. The actual bias-free Harsanyi architecture has zero baseline, where it is valid. The tail expression defines a remainder; its being small is an empirical or cited claim, not a consequence of the M bound.",
                "justification": "",
                "lean_refs": []
              }
