                "id": "hnet-fixed-game",
                "body_md": "Fix a finite universe $N$, model $v$, input $x$ and input baseline vector $r$. The mask $x_T$ retains $x$ on $T$ and uses $r$ elsewhere. Set $g(T)=v(x_T)$, output baseline $b=g(\\varnothing)$ and centered game $g_0(T)=g(T)-b$. The paper's $V(T)$ is $g_0(T)$ and its $I(T)$ is $I_{g_0}(T)$, with empty interaction zero. For unit $j=(l,u)$, set $u_j(T)=z_j(x_T)$; its $J_j(T)$ is the interaction of $u_j-u_j(\\varnothing)$. The source's input baseline $b_i$ corresponds to $r_i$, and differs from the canonical scalar output baseline $b$."
