                "id": "hnet-cnn-equivalence-refuted",
                "title": "Distinguish changing a gate from reindexing",
                "body_md": "For a child vector (1,0), scalar AND requires both coordinates nonzero and is closed; the grouped gate tests their nonzero absolute-value sum and is open. A parent linear value of 1 gives respective outputs 0 and 1, refuting the numerical-equivalence subclaim. The new CNN still has the union-field mask law, so the Shapley argument applies to its own output. Lean proves the grouped-block induction step and gate counterexample. A separate recursive datatype for the entire vector CNN is not yet encoded, and the scalar Expr is not claimed as its full implementation.",
