                "body_md": "Fix the finite universe $N=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$, input $x$, input baseline vector $r$, and a real-valued model $v$. The mask $x_U$ retains coordinates in $U$ and sets the others to $r$; write $g(U)=v(x_U)$ and output baseline $b=g(\\varnothing)$. The source input baseline $b_i$ is distinct from this scalar $b$. Choose one decomposition function $\\gamma$ and put $a(U)=g(U)/2+\\gamma_U$, $o(U)=g(U)/2-\\gamma_U$, so that $a+o=g$. The AND component dividend is $A(S)=\\sum_{U\\subseteq S}(-1)^{|S|-|U|}a(U)$; the nonempty OR component dividend is $O(S)=-\\sum_{U\\subseteq S}(-1)^{|S|-|U|}o(N\\setminus U)$. The raw total-output dividend $I_g$ and component dividend $A$ remain distinct. Local $a=g_{and}$, $o=g_{or}$, $A=I_{g_{and}}$, and $O=O_{g_{or}}$ abbreviate the corresponding public concepts."
