        "translations": {
          "en": {
            "title": "Theorem 3.3: AND/OR allocation for Banzhaf",
            "overview": "Count containment and disjointness events under uniform background subsets.",
            "assumptions": [
              "$N$ is finite. Fix the same input, model, and input baseline. The raw output baseline need not be zero."
            ],
            "definitions": [
              {
                "id": "coalition-objects",
                "body_md": "Fix a finite universe $N$, input $x$, and input baseline vector $r$; put $g(U)=v(x_U)$ and $b=g(\\varnothing)$. Local $a=g_{and}$ and $o=g_{or}$ abbreviate the two source components, $a(U)=g(U)/2+\\gamma_U$ and $o(U)=g(U)/2-\\gamma_U$. Local $A=I_{g_{and}}$ and $O=O_{g_{or}}$ abbreviate the AND component’s Möbius dividend and the nonempty OR negative complementary dividend; $J=A+O$. The raw output baseline need not vanish."
              }
            ],
            "proof_steps": [
              {
                "id": "coalition-banzhaf-step-1",
                "title": "Count uniform background subsets",
                "body_md": "Banzhaf uses uniform background weight $2^{-(n-1)}$. For fixed T containing i, AND requires all other members of T to be present, while OR requires all to be absent. The remaining $n-|T|$ variables are arbitrary, giving $2^{n-|T|}$ backgrounds for either event.",
                "formula_tex": "2^{n-|T|}/2^{n-1}=2^{1-|T|}.",
                "justification": "",
                "lean_refs": [
                  {
                    "declaration": "Harsanyi.Coalition.uniformWeight_superset",
                    "source_path": "lean/HarsanyiLib/Harsanyi/Extensions/CoalitionAttribution.lean",
                    "line": 309,
                    "scope": "uniform_subset_kernel",
                    "explanation_md": "This finite-subset kernel covers containment counts; the formal OR route obtains disjoint-background counts by a complement bijection."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "coalition-banzhaf-step-2",
                "title": "Accumulate AND/OR contributions",
                "body_md": "Interchange finite sums and add the AND and OR contributions. Membership $i\\in N$ and $i\\in T$ ensures $n\\ge1$ and T nonempty.",
                "formula_tex": "B(i)=\\sum_{T\\ni i}2^{1-|T|}J(T).",
                "justification": "",
                "lean_refs": [
                  {
                    "declaration": "PaperCoalition.theorem33",
                    "source_path": "corpus/public/reader/icml2025-coalition/lean/PaperCoalition.lean",
                    "line": 25,
                    "scope": "actual_paper_conclusion",
                    "explanation_md": "Final adapter for the original uniform-marginal Banzhaf value and actual model splitting."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "completion_scope": "Complete mathematical rewriting of the original statement",
            "proof_scope": "Complete mathematical rewriting of the original statement",
            "original_statement_note": "The formulas are aligned with the official PDF. Chinese prose is a project translation; the original layout remains available in the PDF and page evidence.",
            "original_proof_note": "Complete author mathematical calculation, equation by equation. English connective prose is restated faithfully; the source errors remain. This is distinct from the project repair.",
            "original_proof_md": "# Appendix D. Proof of Theorem 3 (main Theorem 3.3)\n\nSource: official PDF pages 14–15. The original names v_and,v_or and original alternating exponents are retained. The displayed exponent +1 differs by two from the common paired form −1, so it is not itself a sign error.\n\nAccording to the AND/OR definitions,\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nI_{and}(S)&=\\sum_{L\\subseteq S}(-1)^{|S|-|L|}v_{and}(L)\n=\\sum_{L\\subseteq S\\setminus\\{i\\}}(-1)^{|S|-|L|+1}[v_{and}(L\\cup\\{i\\})-v_{and}(L)],\\\\\nI_{or}(S)&=-\\sum_{L\\subseteq S}(-1)^{|S|-|L|}v_{or}(N\\setminus L)\n=\\sum_{L\\subseteq S\\setminus\\{i\\}}(-1)^{|S|-|L|+1}[v_{or}(N\\setminus L)-v_{or}(N\\setminus L\\setminus\\{i\\})],\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nwhere v(L)=v_and(L)+v_or(L). Define, solely to keep the long source braces readable,\n\\[\nD(L)=[v_{and}(L\\cup\\{i\\})-v_{and}(L)]+[v_{or}(N\\setminus L)-v_{or}(N\\setminus L\\setminus\\{i\\})].\n\\]\nThe source page-15 chain, with each repeated brace D(L) written in this explicitly defined shorthand, is\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sum_{S\\subseteq N,S\\ni i}\\frac{I_{and}(S)+I_{or}(S)}{2^{|S|-1}}\n&=\\sum_{S\\subseteq N,S\\ni i}\\sum_{L\\subseteq S\\setminus\\{i\\}}\\frac{(-1)^{|S|-|L|+1}}{2^{|S|-1}}D(L)\\\\\n&=\\sum_{S\\subseteq N\\setminus\\{i\\}}\\sum_{L\\subseteq S}\\frac{(-1)^{|S|-|L|}}{2^{|S|}}D(L)\\\\\n&=\\sum_{L\\subseteq N\\setminus\\{i\\}}(-1)^{|L|}\\sum_{\\substack{S\\subseteq N\\setminus\\{i\\}\\\\S\\supseteq L}}\\frac{(-1)^{|S|}}{2^{|S|}}D(L)\\\\\n&=\\sum_{L\\subseteq N\\setminus\\{i\\}}(-1)^{|L|}\\frac{(-1)^{|L|}}{2^{|N|-1}}D(L)\\\\\n&=\\sum_{L\\subseteq N\\setminus\\{i\\}}\\frac1{2^{|N|-1}}D(L)\\\\\n&=\\sum_{S\\subseteq N\\setminus\\{i\\}}\\frac{v_{and}(S\\cup\\{i\\})-v_{and}(S)}{2^{|N|-1}}\n+\\sum_{S\\subseteq N\\setminus\\{i\\}}\\frac{v_{or}(N\\setminus S)-v_{or}(N\\setminus S\\setminus\\{i\\})}{2^{|N|-1}}\\\\\n&=\\sum_{S\\subseteq N\\setminus\\{i\\}}\\frac{v_{and}(S\\cup\\{i\\})-v_{and}(S)}{2^{|N|-1}}\n+\\sum_{S\\subseteq N\\setminus\\{i\\}}\\frac{v_{or}(S\\cup\\{i\\})-v_{or}(S)}{2^{|N|-1}}\\\\\n&=\\sum_{S\\subseteq N\\setminus\\{i\\}}\\frac{[v_{and}(S\\cup\\{i\\})+v_{or}(S\\cup\\{i\\})]-[v_{and}(S)+v_{or}(S)]}{2^{|N|-1}}\\\\\n&=\\sum_{S\\subseteq N\\setminus\\{i\\}}\\frac{v(S\\cup\\{i\\})-v(S)}{2^{|N|-1}}=B(i).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe source comment in the fourth line asserts\n\\[\n\\sum_{\\substack{S\\subseteq N\\setminus\\{i\\}\\\\S\\supseteq L}}\\frac{(-1)^{|S|}}{2^{|S|}}=\\frac{(-1)^{|L|}}{2^{|N|-1}}.\n\\]\nThe last line gives the claimed reformulation.\n"
          }
        },
