                "title": "Eliminate zero interaction terms",
                "body_md": "The prose condition says that both AND and OR effects vanish on every T partially covering S. For any $i\\in S$, a T containing i but not all of S is such a set. Thus each individual conflict term in Theorem 3.6 and every total conflict term in Theorem 3.4 vanishes. The printed set condition has a free i; its intended meaning is explained without silently rewriting its quantifiers.",
                "formula_tex": "\\varphi(i)=\\phi(S)/|S|,\\qquad\\sum_{i\\in S}\\varphi(i)=\\phi(S).",
