                "id": "coalition-objects",
                "body_md": "Fix a finite universe $N$, input $x$, and input baseline vector $r$; put $g(U)=v(x_U)$ and $b=g(\\varnothing)$. Local $a=g_{and}$ and $o=g_{or}$ abbreviate the two source components, $a(U)=g(U)/2+\\gamma_U$ and $o(U)=g(U)/2-\\gamma_U$. Local $A=I_{g_{and}}$ and $O=O_{g_{or}}$ abbreviate the AND component’s Möbius dividend and the nonempty OR negative complementary dividend; $J=A+O$. The raw output baseline need not vanish."
