          "evidence_md": "Let $N=\\{1,2\\}$, $g_1(U)=\\mathbf1[1\\in U]$, $g_2(U)=\\mathbf1[2\\in U]$, and $g=g_1+g_2$. Choose $a_k=g_k,o_k=0$ for the component games. Each has globally minimal L1 value 1 and zero attribution to $N$. For the total game choose $a(U)=\\mathbf1[N\\subseteq U]$, $o(U)=\\mathbf1[U\\ne\\varnothing]$, and thus $\\gamma_U=a(U)-|U|/2$. Its only nonzero interactions are $A(N)=O(N)=1$. Its L1 value 2 reaches the lower bound $|g(N)-g(\\varnothing)|=2$. All three decompositions are globally optimal, yet $\\phi_g(N)=2\\ne0=\\phi_{g_1}(N)+\\phi_{g_2}(N)$.",
